#
# vmapp guest kernel, flavour "gpu" (EXPERIMENTAL): overlay fragment.
#
# Appended AFTER kernel/vmapp-guest.config by kernel/build.sh --flavour gpu, so the lines here win. Together
# with the patch in patches/ this is everything that differs from the default kernel; the required/forbidden
# lists are adjusted next to this file (kconfig-required.txt, kconfig-forbidden.txt) and the reasons are in
# README.md.
#
# Purpose: run a guest with a virtio-gpu device (Venus: Vulkan over virtio-gpu, SPEC section 8.6) on libkrun
# (Hypervisor.framework). The same kernel must still boot under Virtualization.framework, so all virtio over PCI
# options of the base config stay.
#
# Comments must not use the Kconfig "is not set" phrasing (merge_config.sh would parse them as directives).
#

# libkrun describes its virtio devices in the device tree as virtio-mmio nodes (Virtualization.framework uses
# PCI). Devices from the kernel command line (virtio_mmio.device=) stay off: the device tree is the only source.
CONFIG_VIRTIO_MMIO=y
# CONFIG_VIRTIO_MMIO_CMDLINE_DEVICES is not set

# virtio-gpu: the DRM driver with 3D (virgl/venus) contexts and host-visible blobs. No fbdev, no framebuffer
# console, no virtual terminal: nothing in the guest draws, only the user-space Vulkan driver (Mesa Venus) talks
# to /dev/dri/renderD128. SYNC_FILE is the fence file descriptor the driver needs for explicit synchronisation.
CONFIG_DRM=y
CONFIG_DRM_VIRTIO_GPU=y
CONFIG_DRM_VIRTIO_GPU_KMS=y
CONFIG_SYNC_FILE=y
